    "abstractText": "<h4>Background & aims</h4>Delayed diagnosis of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) is associated with worse outcomes. Existing prediction studies often rely on small cohorts or specialized biomarkers that limit scalability. We evaluated whether machine learning models based on routinely collected clinical data can predict future Crohn's disease (CD) and ulcerative colitis (UC) years before diagnosis ",
